The "Before" Plan (The Problem)
Look at the Operation column in the output table. On an unindexed table, you will likely see:

TABLE ACCESS FULL against t_events. This means Oracle is reading every single one of those 1.1 million rows off disk.

SORT ORDER BY or HASH JOIN with a high Cost number, showing that Oracle is struggling to sort the rows or match them up in memory/TEMP space.

After the index:

Run the EXPLAIN PLAN and DBMS_XPLAN.DISPLAY again. You should see:

INDEX RANGE SCAN (or INDEX UNIQUE SCAN) pointing directly to idx_events_trunc_due_person.

No TABLE ACCESS FULL on t_events.

The overall Cost metric should drop dramatically, and the sort operation for pagination will be bypassed because the index is already pre-sorted.
